      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the idea is that all users of SkFont::setupForAsPaths (whose existence I find abhorrent, since it can only cause grief) return the return value separately from the SkStrikeSpec? So this CL currently covers SkStrikeSpec::MakeCanonicalized and then there would need to be one for the other user SkStrikeSpec::MakePath (which is used in two places, the GPU side which involves a little bit of plumbing). Is there a reason to do this in two CLs instead of just doing it all at once since the point is to remove SkStrikeSpec::fStrikeToSourceRatio?\n\nThis pair seems to need to be pushed around enough that it might make sense to give this a name, like an SkScaledStrikeSpec which has a `SkStrikeSpec fStrikeSpec` and a `SkScalar scale`?",
